# sovereign-reth — Agent Context Rules Template
# Copy this file to `GEMINI.md` or `AGENTS.md` in your local environment.

## Source Layout

This is a Rust workspace. All editable source lives under `crates/`, `wallet/src/`,
`wallet/ts/`, `tests/`, `contracts/src/`, `docs/`, `specs/`, and `scripts/`.
Everything else is either generated, a local runtime artifact, or an external dependency.

## Excluded from scanning

Never scan, list, or load the following into context — they are build artifacts
or external dependencies with no editable source content:

| Path | Reason |
|------|--------|
| `target/` | Cargo build artifacts |
| `wallet/target_wasm/` | wasm-pack compilation output |
| `wallet/www/pkg/` | generated wasm-pack JS/WASM output |
| `wallet/pkg/` | wasm-pack staging output |
| `wallet/app/` | bundled frontend output |
| `wallet/dist/` | compiled TypeScript output |
| `wallet/node_modules/` | wallet TypeScript NPM deps |
| `tests/cluster/dist/` | compiled cluster test TypeScript output |
| `contracts/node_modules/` | Solidity toolchain NPM deps |
| `contracts/out/` | Forge compiled artifacts |
| `tests/e2e/node_modules/` | E2E test runner NPM deps |
| `docs/book/` | mdBook compiled documentation |
| `db/`, `db1/`, `db2/` | live RocksDB/MDBX node databases |
| `*.log` | node runtime logs |
| `*.hex` | key files |
| `rustc-ice-*` | compiler crash dumps |
| `Cargo.lock` | auto-generated dependency lock file |

## Load on demand only

Only load the following when the user explicitly asks about them:

- `proposals/` — design document drafts and archives
- `gramine/` — SGX manifest and enclave build files

## Crate naming (for context)

The main crates are:

- `crates/node` — binary entry point + RPC
- `crates/cli` — microservice daemons (gateway, committee, demux)
- `crates/consensus` — Snow family consensus, epoch engine, block-lattice pool
- `crates/identity` — DID resolution, zkp_auth, delegation, W3C ActivityPub
- `crates/attestation` — SGX attestation pipeline
- `crates/network` — P2P networking, DAS, WireGuard, signal swarm
- `crates/crypto` — cryptographic profiles and signature schemes (ML-DSA, Falcon, Secp256k1)
- `wallet/` — WASM wallet & TypeScript SDK (EIP-8141 envelope, debugger, CAIP-25)
